+/// (QuickTerm) Whether the mouse modifiers currently held are the ones that make a click a
+/// *link* click: the OSC 8 modifiers (Ctrl, or Super on macOS) or the modifiers of any
+/// configured link. Used to let a link click through even while the program has mouse
+/// reporting on — a Cmd-click on a URL in a TUI is far more often "open this" than input meant
+/// for the program — and the click is then swallowed before it is reported (mirroring the
+/// Shift override), so the program does not also act on it.
+///
+/// Reads only the raw mods, so it needs no lock; Shift held rules a link click out anyway.
+fn mouseModsWantLink(self: *const Surface) bool {
+    const mods = self.mouse.mods;
+    if (mods.equal(input.ctrlOrSuper(.{}))) return true;
+    for (self.config.links) |link| switch (link.highlight) {
+        .always_mods, .hover_mods => |v| if (v.equal(mods)) return true,
+        .always, .hover => {},
+    };
+    return false;
+}
